values ('b7c8d9e0-1f2a-4b12-9c41-5d6e7f8a9b02', 'food-and-beverage-management', 'Food and Beverage Management', 'This course develops the operational and managerial competence required to plan, run, control, and improve food and beverage businesses. Students integrate concept development, market fit, menu design, purchasing, inventory, kitchen production, food safety, beverage management, service, catering, facilities, labor, finance, revenue, technology, marketing, sustainability, ethics, and risk. Applications span restaurants, bars, hotels, resorts, clubs, events, institutional foodservice, and off-premise channels. A semester project requires an executable restaurant concept or improvement proposal supported by operational plans, controls, financial analysis, and measurable evaluation.');

